# Force LF line endings for all text files regardless of the checkout
# platform's git config. Without this, GitHub's windows-latest runners
# (core.autocrlf=true by default there) silently convert every LF in a
# checked-out text file to CRLF, changing its byte content -- confirmed
# directly via CI: app/web/style.css checked out at 86259 bytes on
# windows-latest vs. 85572 bytes as stored in the repo, a difference of
# exactly 687 bytes = the file's 687 LF line endings each becoming CRLF.
# That silently broke tests/original_plus_test.py's byte-exact comparison
# there while passing everywhere else, and would affect any other exact
# byte/hash comparison (or the actual shipped app reading its own web/
# source files) the same way.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Real binary files: never touch line endings in these.
android/keystore/debug.keystore binary
android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar binary
windows_build/icon/app.ico binary
windows_build/*/rsrc_windows_amd64.syso binary
